 "note": "The Weld Theatre (Weld Hall Theatre, from 1874; Victorian Italianate, brick, corrugated iron roof; inHerit), 13 Queen St on the Adelaide St corner, kept beside Saltwater and joined to it behind (City of Busselton: an upgraded back of house, a scene dock leveller and a new covered courtyard behind the old theatre). From the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026); no photo of the street front was found, so the front, colours and the parapet are guesses. A hipped hall with its ridge along Queen St, a gabled entrance porch pushing out to the street, a taller gabled stage house behind and a gabled side wing to Adelaide St; behind them the two long low roofs of the back-of-house and the covered courtyard, marked as outbuildings. Plain lettering only. Metres: x left to right as seen from Queen St (north to south), y back (east) from the porch front.",
